'''Hoechst Schering AgrEvo [[Gesellschaft mit beschränkter Haftung|GmbH]]''' was a [[Düsseldorf]]-based [[limited liability company]] owned by [[Hoechst AG]] and [[Schering AG]] that only existed as an independent company for five years, from 1994 to 1999.<ref name="Bijman 2001">{{cite journal |author=Bijman, Jos |year=2001 |title=AgroEvo: from crop protection to crop production |journal=AgBioForum |volume=4 |issue=1 |pages=20–25 |url=http://www.agbioforum.org/v4n1/v4n1a04-bijman.pdf}}</ref>

It was established in 1994, when two [[Germany|German]] producers of chemicals and pharmaceuticals, Hoechst and Schering, merged their crop protection divisions into a new joint venture to benefit from economies of scale in marketing and research and development.<ref name="Bijman 2001"/> In 1999, AgrEvo’s majority shareholder, Hoechst, merged with the [[France|French]] pharmaceutical and chemical company [[Rhône-Poulenc]] to become [[Aventis]], with AgrEvo and Rhône-Poulenc's agrochemicals division combined into Aventis CropScience.<ref name="Bijman 2001"/> In 2002, [[Bayer|Bayer AG]] acquired Aventis CropScience and combined it with their agrochemicals division (Bayer Pflanzenschutz or "Crop Protection") to form [[Bayer|Bayer CropScience]].

== Products ==
* Unim Plus, a [[weedicide]] for vegetables, tea, and cotton<ref name="agrevo">''Hoechst Schering AgrEvo: Protecting Investors too'', ''Economic Times'', {{ISSN|0013-0389}}, 1998.</ref> 
* Puma, a super [[herbicide]] for wheat<ref name="agrevo"/>

